from pathlib import Path
import nbformat
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
TAG='broad-descriptor-audit-20261030'
def install():
    p=ROOT/"synthetic_experiments/notebooks/synthetic_predictor_validation.ipynb"
    n=nbformat.read(p,4)
    n.cells=[c for c in n.cells if TAG not in c.metadata.get("tags",[])]
    cells=[
        nbformat.v4.new_markdown_cell('## 8. Geometry-only descriptor audit — width, length, slope and topology\n\n**SYN-GEOMETRY-ONLY-DESCRIPTORS-2026-10-30.** The preceding sections explain the selected ten; they do not prove those ten are optimal. This supporting audit evaluates a broader, pre-existing library on the completed synthetic grid. Earlier hydraulic diagnostics remain historical context. This active candidate screen excludes resistance and inverse-depth ΔG; Manning ΔG is included as a geometry/slope candidate; all rankings, coverage counts and matrices below use geometry and slope only.\n\nThere are **205 candidate representations**, not 205 independent concepts: 37 non-hydraulic DAG metrics with the existing parent/child/difference/ratio forms; historical complete-path metrics including equivalent length/width, elongation and signed length–width association; reference slope/head summaries; the geometry-only members of the current predictors; and the new spread/entropy differences. Only existing ratio forms are included; no exhaustive products or powers are generated.\n\nThe 137,781 comparisons cover all three depth methods. Most geometric values use the same closed outer B domains; Manning ΔG explicitly uses whole-network sums. Historical complete-path harmonic-width weights are **not the same as routed discharge fractions**, and their equivalent-length/entropy definitions are labelled separately. The original fitted model is preserved; its resistance and inverse-depth ΔG inputs are excluded from this candidate analysis. No routing, RF fitting, subset search, or production-model replacement is performed.\n\nSome metrics are deferred explicitly: old omega/exposure/length-fraction definitions need domain reconciliation; routed celerity/travel-time/diffusivity/dispersion measures are not silently mixed into this geometric screen; pixel-width and map-shape metrics lack synthetic observations. See `deferred_inventory` below.\n\n### 8a. What can this grid actually evaluate?\n\nA descriptor constant within each type may still distinguish different topology types. It is **not rejected as uninformative**; this within-type factorial analysis cannot measure its response to the eight controls. Partially defined candidates are retained with their coverage, rather than imputed.'),
        nbformat.v4.new_code_cell("import geometry_only_descriptor_audit as broad\nbroad_path=broad.OUT\nbroad_provenance=json.loads((broad_path/'provenance.json').read_text())\nfor path,digest in broad_provenance['source_sha256'].items():\n    assert hashlib.sha256(Path(path).read_bytes()).hexdigest()==digest, f'Changed broad-audit source: {path}'\ncorrelation_provenance=json.loads((broad_path/'control_correlations_provenance.json').read_text())\nfor path,digest in correlation_provenance['source_sha256'].items():\n    assert hashlib.sha256(Path(path).read_bytes()).hexdigest()==digest, f'Changed control-association source: {path}'\nBROAD_METHOD='variable_manning'\nbroad_catalog=pd.read_csv(broad_path/'candidate_catalog.csv')\nassert len(broad_catalog)==205\nassert not set(broad_catalog.variable)&broad.EXCLUDED\nbroad_coverage=pd.read_csv(broad_path/'coverage.csv')\nbroad_effects=pd.read_csv(broad_path/'factorial_signatures.csv')\nbroad_summary=pd.read_csv(broad_path/'exploratory_summary.csv')\nbroad_controls=pd.read_csv(broad_path/'control_correlations.csv')\naffine_aliases=pd.read_csv(broad_path/'affine_aliases.csv')\ndeferred_inventory=pd.read_csv(broad_path/'deferred_inventory.csv')\nstatus=broad_coverage[broad_coverage.method==BROAD_METHOD].groupby('variable').agg(min_finite_pct=('finite_pct','min'),max_finite_pct=('finite_pct','max'),varying_types=('status',lambda x:int((x=='varying').sum())))\nstatus['assessment']=['Undefined throughout' if hi==0 else 'Partly defined' if lo<100 else 'Constant within every type' if k==0 else 'Fully defined; varies within a type' for lo,hi,k in zip(status.min_finite_pct,status.max_finite_pct,status.varying_types)]\nstatus=status.reset_index().merge(broad_catalog,on='variable',validate='one_to_one')\ndisplay(status.groupby('assessment').size().rename('candidate representations').to_frame())\nfamily_inventory=pd.crosstab(status.family,status.assessment)\nax=family_inventory.plot.barh(stacked=True,figsize=(12,7),color=['#94a3b8','#2563eb','#f59e0b'][:len(family_inventory.columns)])\nax.set(xlabel='Number of candidate representations',ylabel='',title='Broader descriptor inventory · '+BROAD_METHOD)\nax.legend(title='Within-type assessment',bbox_to_anchor=(1.02,1),loc='upper left');display_figure(ax.figure);plt.close(ax.figure)\nprint('Catalog:',len(broad_catalog),'representations. Affine aliases detected on full variable-Manning grid:',len(affine_aliases))\ndisplay(pd.read_csv(broad_path/'excluded_candidates.csv')[['variable','exclusion_reason']])\ndisplay(deferred_inventory)\nSHOW_FULL_CATALOG=False\nif SHOW_FULL_CATALOG:display(status)\n"),
        nbformat.v4.new_markdown_cell("### 8b. What emerges from the broader screen?\n\nThe table is a **descriptive association screen on the same full grid**, not held-out predictive performance. It averages absolute within-type Spearman correlations equally over the six response-resolved types. Sign can differ by type; inspect `response_associations.csv` for signed values. Only candidates complete and nonconstant in all six response-resolved types enter this ranking. Partial/constant candidates remain in the inventory and mechanism matrices; they are not rejected.\n\nResistance and inverse-depth ΔG are excluded. **Manning ΔG is included**: whole-network sums of L B^(2/5) f^(3/5) S^(-3/10), child minus parent. Width/connectivity-derived f is recomputed per state; no roughness, depth or simulated discharge is used. Its physical interpretation remains conditional on Manning hydraulics. The parent inverse-square-root slope descriptor remains: it depends on slope and geometric allocation only. Reported affine aliases can be hidden to reduce repetition, but this is not full redundancy analysis: nonlinear monotonic duplicates can remain. A high association does not establish unique added information or justify selecting ten inputs retrospectively.\n\nCompare centroid and peak rankings, then use the original control/interaction matrices below to understand the candidate's mechanisms. Model selection, grouped held-out prediction, and real-network transfer remain separate tasks."),
        nbformat.v4.new_code_cell("HIDE_REPORTED_AFFINE_ALIASES=True\nTOP_CANDIDATES=18\nresponse_resolved_counts=coverage[(coverage.method==BROAD_METHOD)&coverage.variable.isin(RESPONSES)&coverage.resolved].groupby('variable').size()\nfor response in RESPONSES:\n    candidates=broad_summary[(broad_summary.method==BROAD_METHOD)&(broad_summary.response==response)].copy()\n    count=int(response_resolved_counts.get(response,0))\n    candidates=candidates[(candidates.types_with_correlation==count)&candidates.min_finite_pct.eq(100)&candidates.role.ne('analytical reference')]\n    if HIDE_REPORTED_AFFINE_ALIASES:candidates=candidates[~candidates.variable.isin(affine_aliases.variable)]\n    candidates['in_current_ten']=candidates.variable.isin(CURRENT_PREDICTORS)\n    candidates=candidates.sort_values('mean_abs_spearman',ascending=False)\n    print(RESPONSES[response],': complete varying candidates across',count,'resolved types')\n    display(candidates[['variable','family','role','mean_abs_spearman','types_with_correlation','in_current_ten']].head(TOP_CANDIDATES).round(3))\nprint('These are descriptive correlations, not R² or evidence of added predictive information.')\n"),
        nbformat.v4.new_markdown_cell('### 8c. The same control and interaction matrices for a broader family\n\nSelect any catalog family; no candidates are omitted from that family. Default: **shape/path-width**, which includes equivalent length, equivalent width, elongation and signed length–width association in parent, child and difference forms. These are useful additions to the original shortlist.\n\nRows are controls/pairs and columns are candidates, exactly as in Section 7. Overall mode averages within-type summaries; available types can differ across candidates, so inspect coverage. Undefined or constant factorial signatures remain gray. The Spearman view uses finite pairs and can therefore cover a restricted grid. All 205 representations and all 28 pair interactions are exported; the family selector only limits plot size.'),
        nbformat.v4.new_code_cell("BROAD_FAMILY='shape/path-width'  # options: sorted(broad_catalog.family.unique())\nBROAD_SCOPE='overall'  # or 'selected_type', using CONTROL_TREATMENT\nfamily_columns=broad_catalog[broad_catalog.family==BROAD_FAMILY].variable.tolist()\nassert family_columns, sorted(broad_catalog.family.unique())\nselected_c=broad_controls[(broad_controls.method==BROAD_METHOD)&broad_controls.variable.isin(family_columns)]\nselected_e=broad_effects[(broad_effects.method==BROAD_METHOD)&broad_effects.variable.isin(family_columns)]\nselected_status=broad_coverage[(broad_coverage.method==BROAD_METHOD)&broad_coverage.variable.isin(family_columns)]\nif BROAD_SCOPE=='selected_type':\n    selected_c=selected_c[selected_c.child_state==CONTROL_TREATMENT]\n    selected_e=selected_e[selected_e.child_state==CONTROL_TREATMENT]\n    selected_status=selected_status[selected_status.child_state==CONTROL_TREATMENT]\nelif BROAD_SCOPE!='overall':raise ValueError(BROAD_SCOPE)\nlabels={c:c.replace('B_','').replace('path_','path: ',1).replace('_',' ') for c in family_columns}\nimport itertools\nfor title,frame,row,value,order,signed in [\n    ('Spearman association',selected_c,'factor','spearman',list(FACTOR_LABELS),True),\n    ('Main-effect variance contribution',selected_e[selected_e.order==1],'term','variance_pct',list(FACTOR_LABELS),False),\n    ('All pair-interaction variance contributions',selected_e[selected_e.order==2],'term','variance_pct',[' × '.join(x) for x in itertools.combinations(FACTOR_LABELS,2)],False)]:\n    mat=frame.pivot_table(index=row,columns='variable',values=value,aggfunc='mean').reindex(index=order,columns=family_columns)\n    fig=pam.figure(mat,'Broad audit · '+BROAD_FAMILY+' · '+title,labels,FACTOR_LABELS,signed=signed)\n    fig.set_size_inches(max(14,len(family_columns)*.95),max(5,len(order)*.43))\n    fig.axes[-1].set_ylabel('Spearman correlation' if signed else '% of predictor variance')\n    display_figure(fig);plt.close(fig)\ndisplay(selected_status.groupby('variable').agg(min_finite_pct=('finite_pct','min'),varying_types=('status',lambda x:int((x=='varying').sum()))))\n")
    ]
    for c in cells:c.metadata["tags"]=[TAG]
    n.cells.extend(cells);nbformat.write(n,p)
if __name__=="__main__":install()
